(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase474OneProjectionManySurfaces"
  :createdAt 1789370000000
  :status "done" :completedAt 1789400400000
  :priorityOrder 2
  :summary "One Projection, Many Surfaces: launcher and skills draw the same content from one source through one mechanism, each declaring only what is genuinely its own."
  :phase "Phase474OneProjectionManySurfaces"
  :baseline "Measured 2026-09-12. The rule source is projected into four different shapes by scripts/install.sh: a comment delimited block in AGENTS.md, a single quoted bash string in the launcher, a fenced asn block in SKILL.md, and a derived rules list in skill.asn, each with its own delimiters and escaping. The source is therefore constrained by the weakest of the four, which is why it may contain no apostrophe. Twenty skills exist under .agents/skills and exactly one of them, asl-toolbelt, carries the rules; the other nineteen receive nothing. Two skill trees disagree: the root holds 20 skills and asl/.agents/skills holds 22, and gate 7 prefers the nested tree, reporting 22 audited and describing them as fresh while the renderer writes to both. The launcher is 937 lines of which the genuinely launcher specific part is client targeting for five clients, two strict Claude invariants that convert a system prompt overwrite into an append and strip dangerous permissions, and the orchestration flags; the rest is content it shares with every skill."
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task47401" :parentId "" :phase "phase-474"
      :title "One projection: content, shape, destination"
      :kind :engine :state :done :lane "projection" :priority :critical :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789370000000 :updatedAt 1789399800000
      :motivation "The same rules are rendered four ways by four pieces of shell, and each rendering imposes its own escaping on the source. A bash single quoted string is why the rule text may contain no apostrophe: the weakest consumer sets the vocabulary of the thing everything else reads. Four renderings also mean four ways to drift and four drift checks to maintain, one per shape rather than one per fact."
      :purpose "One mechanism in the binary produces a projection from three declared parts: what content, being a rule tier, a capability slice for a situation, or the lexicon; in what shape, being a delimited block, a fenced block, or a record; and to what destination. The launcher and every skill are callers of it with different arguments rather than four implementations. Escaping belongs to the shape and never to the source, so the source is free of any consumer's syntax."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["One projection mechanism, three declared parts" "Escaping owned by the shape, not the source" "The apostrophe prohibition retired" "Four renderers reduced to callers"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" "scripts/install.sh" "asl/grammar/rules.asn"]
      :targetSymbols ["render_between" "inject_directive" "run_launch"] :relatedSymbols ["ssot" "budget" "output"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task47007"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47401"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47401.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A rule containing an apostrophe and a double quote projects correctly into every shape." "One content selector produces byte identical meaning in all three shapes, differing only in delimiters." "Adding a destination requires no new renderer." "A projection requested at a tier contains that tier and no more."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47401" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task47401" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47401" :assertCount 15 :at 1789399800000)] :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Define the three parts." "Implement once in the binary." "Convert the four renderers to callers." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 3 :receipts [(:receipt :step 3 :status :ok :hash "dac75da")])
    (:task
      :id "Task47402" :parentId "" :phase "phase-474"
      :title "Skills draw from the projection, and there is one skill tree"
      :kind :remediation :state :done :lane "projection" :priority :critical :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789370000000 :updatedAt 1789400000000
      :motivation "One skill of twenty carries the rules. The other nineteen are activated by an agent that then has no access to the constraints it is working under, unless it happens to have loaded the one that does. Meanwhile two skill trees disagree by two entries, the renderer writes to both and gate 7 audits only the nested one, so the tree an agent reads and the tree the gate checks are not the same tree."
      :purpose "A skill declares which projection it needs rather than embedding a copy, so a skill that needs the rules gets the current rules and a skill that needs only a capability slice carries only that. One tree is canonical and the other is derived from it or removed. What a skill embeds is its own body and its trigger; everything shared arrives by reference."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Every skill declares the projection it needs" "Shared content arrives by reference, never embedded" "One canonical skill tree" "The tree the gate audits is the tree an agent reads"]
      :owns [".agents/skills" "asl/.agents/skills" "scripts/install.sh"]
      :targetSymbols [] :relatedSymbols ["ssot" "capabilities" "budget"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task47401"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47402"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47402.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A rule change is visible to every skill that declared the rules, with no skill file edited." "A skill embedding a copy of shared content fails the check." "Two skill trees holding different sets fails." "A skill declaring a projection that does not exist fails."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47402" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task47402" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47402" :assertCount 37 :at 1789400000000)] :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Give each skill a declared projection." "Reconcile the two trees to one." "Forbid embedded copies." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 4 :receipts [(:receipt :step 4 :status :ok :hash "HEAD")])
    (:task
      :id "Task47403" :parentId "" :phase "phase-474"
      :title "What is the launcher's own is declared as its own"
      :kind :engine :state :done :lane "projection" :priority :high :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789370000000 :updatedAt 1789400200000
      :motivation "Most of the launcher is content it shares with every skill, and a small part is genuinely its own: which client is being started, where that client reads its channel, the orchestration limits, and the two invariants that keep a Claude session from having its base prompt overwritten or its permission model bypassed. Those have already been lost once by being tangled with the shared part, when a build overwrote the file that carried both."
      :purpose "The launcher declares its own concerns separately from the projection it requests: the client target and its channel location, the orchestration flags, workspace discovery, and the client specific invariants. Each invariant is a named, tested rule rather than a branch inside an argument loop, so porting or refactoring cannot quietly drop one."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Launcher specifics declared separately from shared content" "Each client invariant named and tested individually" "Adding a client requires no change to the projection" "An invariant cannot be dropped without a case failing"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" "asl/grammar/protocol-conformance.asn"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_launch" "find_workspace_root"] :relatedSymbols ["capabilities" "foreign" "edge"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task47006" "Task47401"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47403"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47403.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Each declared client invariant has its own case that fails when the invariant is removed." "Adding a sixth client requires no change to the projection mechanism." "A client declared without a channel location fails rather than defaulting silently."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47403" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task47403" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47403" :assertCount 16 :at 1789400200000)] :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Separate own concerns from requested content." "Name and test each invariant." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 3 :receipts [(:receipt :step 3 :status :ok :hash "HEAD")])
    (:task
      :id "Task47404" :parentId "" :phase "phase-474"
      :title "Gate 7 checks currency, not population"
      :kind :engine :state :done :lane "projection" :priority :high :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789370000000 :updatedAt 1789400400000
      :motivation "Gate 7 counts skills in whichever tree it finds first, reports twenty two, and calls their frontmatters and trigger descriptions fresh. Freshness against what is not stated and not computed: nineteen of twenty skills carry no rules at all, so there is nothing in them that could be stale, and the one that does is checked by a different mechanism. A gate that reports a population as fresh is counting, not checking."
      :purpose "Gate 7 verifies that every skill's declared projection matches what the source currently produces, and reports how many skills it checked against how many exist. A skill whose projection is out of date fails, and a tree the gate did not look at is reported rather than skipped."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Currency verified against the source" "Checked count reported against existing count" "An unexamined tree reported, not skipped" "The freshness claim backed by a comparison"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_gate_7_skills"] :relatedSymbols ["gates" "output" "ssot"]
      :invariants ["D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task47402" "Task47005"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47404"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47404.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Changing the source without reprojecting makes gate 7 fail." "The gate reports the count it checked and the count that exists, and they agree or it fails." "A second tree present but unexamined is reported."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47404" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task47404" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47404" :assertCount 12 :at 1789400400000)] :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Compare projection against source." "Report checked against existing." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 3 :receipts [(:receipt :step 3 :status :ok :hash "HEAD")])]
  :notes "The organising idea is that the launcher and a skill differ in what they ask for and where it goes, not in how it is produced. Once the projection is one mechanism reading one source, the launcher keeps only client targeting, orchestration flags and its client invariants, and a skill keeps only its body and its trigger.")
